    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399-a1">

                <pb facs="0567" n="461" xml:id="pg461"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Sleeper to the Secretary of State and
                        Justice.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-08-28"><hi rendition="#small-caps">August</hi> 28,
                            1906</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to
                    respectfully request that your excellency’s Government immediately take the
                    necessary steps for the protection of the following American interests, in the
                    province of Santa Clara, now jeopardized by acts of the insurgents:</p>
                <p>The Colonial Sugar Company (Constancia) Mr. R. B. Childs. The Hormi-guero Central
                    Company, of Hormiguero. The Trinidad Plantation, Mr. S. M. Patterson. The Cuba
                    Cattle and Land Company, Trinidad, Mr. H. S. Ismon.</p>
                <p>Trusting that there may be no delay in complying with my request, I avail myself
                    of this opportunity to renew to your excellency the assurance of my highest
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>(Signed) <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacob Sleeper</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
